.. Shared fragment: the sorted-batch promise. Included by every language guide;
   edit here, not in the guides.

The sorted path skips treeweave's internal bin-sort and is ~3-4x faster on an
ascending 1-D batch, which covers regular grids, quadrature nodes, time series
and parameter sweeps. The caller promises ``x[i] <= x[i+1]``, and treeweave
does not verify the promise, so unsorted input yields wrong values. Use the
plain batch path when the order is unknown. It sorts internally and is always
correct.
